        <section id="bugs-in-code"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
            <h2>Bugs in Code</h2>
              <p>Developers will write unit tests for their code to make sure it works correctly, and this can help to prevent against bugs. Software bugs are errors or flaws in computer programs or systems.</p>
<p>So what exactly is meant by bugs in relation to code?</p>

              
              <!-- IF 2 --><ul class="l-icon-grid ">
  
  
    
    <!--  -->
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u4_s2_p2_reveal1.svg" alt="Syntax error" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Syntax error</h3>
      <p>This is when the syntax is incorrect, such as missing end of line characters/indents, unrecognised characters or variable names, or incorrect case sensitivity.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u4_s2_p2_reveal2.svg" alt="Runtime errors" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Runtime errors</h3>
      <p>Runtime errors occur when a program is run or executed. They can be caused by problems such as infinite loops, memory leaks, or corrupt files.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u4_s2_p2_reveal3.svg" alt="Semantic (also known as logic errors)" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Semantic (also known as logic errors)</h3>
      <p>These occur when no error message is created, but the functionality is not what the programmer intended. For example, when datatypes are not converted correctly (such as float to int), or inadvertently using a function name as a variable name.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
      
  
  
    
  
  <li class="c-reveal-block">
    <img class="c-reveal-block__icon js-showhide" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u4_s2_p2_reveal4.svg" alt="Compilation" width="266" height="266">
    
    <div class="c-reveal-block__desc">
      <h3 aria-hidden="true">Compilation</h3>
      <p>This is when there is an error for the building the machine code for the program, most commonly caused by basic syntax errors.</p>

    </div>
  </li>
  
</ul>

            
              <p>When there is a bug in the code, this can cause the program to crash, function incorrectly, or become non-functional.</p>

          
